<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<definitions xmlns="https://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20191111/MODEL/" xmlns:dmndi="https://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20191111/DMNDI/" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20180521/DC/" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20180521/DI/" id="Jurisdictional_boundary" name="17.3.4 Confirm jurisdictional and regulated-segment boundaries" namespace="http://tim-method.example/utility-wam/1.0" exporter="Utility WAM Industry Process Reference" exporterVersion="2026-08-28">
  <description>Returns A JURISDICTION AND THE STATUTE OR PART THAT SET IT, never a list of obligations. Every other model in this category and several in 8.0 consume this value, which is why it is a table of its own rather than a paragraph in each of them.

The electric half is the asymmetry that runs through this whole reference. 16 U.S.C. 824o(a)(1) says the bulk-power system does not include facilities used in the local distribution of electric energy, and 824o(i)(1) limits the Electric Reliability Organization to reliability standards for the bulk-power system. So the NERC TPL and PRC families are named in 17.2.3 ONLY where this table has returned bulkPower - the same discipline 7.0 applies to FAC-003, where the citation is a negative finding rather than an obligation.

The gas half is 49 CFR 192.3's definitions of transmission line and distribution line, 192.8 and 192.9 for gathering, and the resulting split between Subpart O and Subpart P. Gas has a federal layer here that electric distribution does not, and that is a fact about the law rather than an omission in the model.</description>
  <inputData id="in_commodity" name="Commodity"><variable id="in_commodity_v" name="Commodity" typeRef="string"/></inputData>
  <inputData id="in_electricRole" name="Electric facility role"><variable id="in_electricRole_v" name="Electric facility role" typeRef="string"/></inputData>
  <inputData id="in_gasLineType" name="Gas line type under 49 CFR 192.3"><variable id="in_gasLineType_v" name="Gas line type under 49 CFR 192.3" typeRef="string"/></inputData>
  <knowledgeSource id="ks_jurisdiction" name="16 U.S.C. 824o(a)(1) and (i)(1); 49 CFR 192.3, 192.8, 192.9 and 192.1001"><description>824o(a)(1) excludes local distribution from the bulk-power system and (i)(1) limits the ERO to it. 192.3 defines transmission and distribution lines; 192.8 and 192.9 govern gathering; 192.1001 opens Subpart P.</description></knowledgeSource>
  <decision id="d_17_3_4" name="Jurisdiction">
    <variable id="d_17_3_4_v" name="Jurisdiction" typeRef="string"/>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_d_17_3_4_ks_jurisdiction"><requiredInput href="#ks_jurisdiction"/></informationRequirement>
    <decisionTable id="d_17_3_4_dt" hitPolicy="FIRST" preferredOrientation="Rule-as-Row">
      <input id="d_17_3_4_i1" label="Commodity"><inputExpression id="d_17_3_4_i1_e" typeRef="string"><text>in_commodity</text></inputExpression></input>
      <input id="d_17_3_4_i2" label="Electric facility role"><inputExpression id="d_17_3_4_i2_e" typeRef="string"><text>in_electricRole</text></inputExpression></input>
      <input id="d_17_3_4_i3" label="Gas line type"><inputExpression id="d_17_3_4_i3_e" typeRef="string"><text>in_gasLineType</text></inputExpression></input>
      <output id="d_17_3_4_o" label="Jurisdiction" name="Jurisdiction" typeRef="string"/>
      <rule id="d_17_3_4_r1">
        <description>16 U.S.C. 824o(a)(1). Outside the bulk-power system, so outside the ERO's standards under (i)(1). There is no federal reliability layer here; the obligations, where they exist, are the State's.</description>
        <inputEntry id="d_17_3_4_r1_ie1"><text>"electric"</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_17_3_4_r1_ie2"><text>"localDistribution"</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_17_3_4_r1_ie3"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_17_3_4_r1_oe"><text>"localDistribution"</text></outputEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="d_17_3_4_r2">
        <description>16 U.S.C. 824o. NERC TPL and PRC families apply and 17.2.3 names them. This is the only branch in which they may be cited as binding.</description>
        <inputEntry id="d_17_3_4_r2_ie1"><text>"electric"</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_17_3_4_r2_ie2"><text>"bulkPower"</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_17_3_4_r2_ie3"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_17_3_4_r2_oe"><text>"bulkPower"</text></outputEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="d_17_3_4_r3">
        <description>49 CFR 192.3 transmission line; Subpart O transmission integrity management, with 17.3.3 deciding whether a given segment is covered.</description>
        <inputEntry id="d_17_3_4_r3_ie1"><text>"gas"</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_17_3_4_r3_ie2"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_17_3_4_r3_ie3"><text>"transmission"</text></inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_17_3_4_r3_oe"><text>"part192SubpartO"</text></outputEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="d_17_3_4_r4">
        <description>49 CFR 192.3 distribution line; 192.1001 to 192.1015 distribution integrity management. Not Subpart O, at any class location.</description>
        <inputEntry id="d_17_3_4_r4_ie1"><text>"gas"</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_17_3_4_r4_ie2"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_17_3_4_r4_ie3"><text>"distribution"</text></inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_17_3_4_r4_oe"><text>"part192SubpartP"</text></outputEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="d_17_3_4_r5">
        <description>49 CFR 192.8 and 192.9. How much of Part 192 applies depends on the gathering type, and this reference does not state that determination.</description>
        <inputEntry id="d_17_3_4_r5_ie1"><text>"gas"</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_17_3_4_r5_ie2"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_17_3_4_r5_ie3"><text>"gathering"</text></inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_17_3_4_r5_oe"><text>"part192Gathering"</text></outputEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="d_17_3_4_r6">
        <description>Commodity or line type not established. Everything downstream of this table depends on it, so a named exception is better than a default.</description>
        <inputEntry id="d_17_3_4_r6_ie1"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_17_3_4_r6_ie2"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_17_3_4_r6_ie3"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_17_3_4_r6_oe"><text>"determineManually"</text></outputEntry>
      </rule>
    </decisionTable>
  </decision>
  <dmndi:DMNDI>
    <dmndi:DMNDiagram id="drd_Jurisdictional_boundary">
      <dmndi:DMNShape id="sh_in_commodity" dmnElementRef="in_commodity"><dc:Bounds x="60" y="420" width="160" height="45"/></dmndi:DMNShape>
      <dmndi:DMNShape id="sh_in_electricRole" dmnElementRef="in_electricRole"><dc:Bounds x="245" y="420" width="160" height="45"/></dmndi:DMNShape>
      <dmndi:DMNShape id="sh_in_gasLineType" dmnElementRef="in_gasLineType"><dc:Bounds x="430" y="420" width="160" height="45"/></dmndi:DMNShape>
      <dmndi:DMNShape id="sh_d_17_3_4" dmnElementRef="d_17_3_4"><dc:Bounds x="60" y="240" width="180" height="70"/></dmndi:DMNShape>
      <dmndi:DMNShape id="sh_ks_jurisdiction" dmnElementRef="ks_jurisdiction"><dc:Bounds x="900" y="100" width="160" height="55"/></dmndi:DMNShape>
    </dmndi:DMNDiagram>
  </dmndi:DMNDI>
</definitions>
